Subject: [PATCH] Android: reset the hovered accessibility node on ACTION_HOVER_EXIT

On a lift of the finger QtAccessibilityDelegate kept the node under it as the hovered one,
so the next touch on the same node sent TalkBack no TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_ENTER, and TalkBack did
not focus it again once a swipe had moved the focus elsewhere. Reset it and send
TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_EXIT, as ExploreByTouchHelper of AndroidX does (the same code is still in
Qt 6.8 and dev). setHoveredVirtualViewId sends no hover exit when no node was hovered, so
the touch after a lift logs no "sendEventForVirtualViewId for invalid view". Applied to qtbase v5.15.0; jar/QtAndroid.jar is built with build_qtandroid_jar.sh.
---
--- a/src/android/jar/src/org/qtproject/qt5/android/accessibility/QtAccessibilityDelegate.java
+++ b/src/android/jar/src/org/qtproject/qt5/android/accessibility/QtAccessibilityDelegate.java
@@ -184,7 +184,19 @@
                 setHoveredVirtualViewId(virtualViewId);
                 break;
             case MotionEvent.ACTION_HOVER_EXIT:
-                setHoveredVirtualViewId(virtualViewId);
+                // The finger lifted: no node is hovered any more, as ExploreByTouchHelper of
+                // AndroidX does. Kept as hovered, the node got no TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_ENTER on the next
+                // touch on it (setHoveredVirtualViewId sends nothing for the same node), and
+                // TalkBack did not focus it again once a swipe had moved the focus elsewhere.
+                // Not through setHoveredVirtualViewId(INVALID_ID): it would also send a hover enter
+                // for the invalid view, which sendEventForVirtualViewId drops with a warning.
+                // The next touch starts from INVALID_ID, so setHoveredVirtualViewId skips the
+                // hover exit for it.
+                if (m_hoveredVirtualViewId != INVALID_ID) {
+                    final int previousVirtualViewId = m_hoveredVirtualViewId;
+                    m_hoveredVirtualViewId = INVALID_ID;
+                    sendEventForVirtualViewId(previousVirtualViewId, AccessibilityEvent.TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_EXIT);
+                }
                 break;
         }
 
@@ -223,7 +235,11 @@
         final int previousVirtualViewId = m_hoveredVirtualViewId;
         m_hoveredVirtualViewId = virtualViewId;
         sendEventForVirtualViewId(virtualViewId, AccessibilityEvent.TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_ENTER);
-        sendEventForVirtualViewId(previousVirtualViewId, AccessibilityEvent.TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_EXIT);
+        // No node was hovered (the first touch, or the finger lifted): nothing to exit, as in
+        // ExploreByTouchHelper; sendEventForVirtualViewId would only log a warning for it.
+        if (previousVirtualViewId != INVALID_ID) {
+            sendEventForVirtualViewId(previousVirtualViewId, AccessibilityEvent.TYPE_VIEW_HOVER_EXIT);
+        }
     }
 
     private AccessibilityEvent getEventForVirtualViewId(int virtualViewId, int eventType)
